"},{"id":2,"category":"盈利能力","desc":"營業現金流 CFO > 0","passed":1,"detail":"自由現金流 = $406M"},{"id":3,"category":"盈利能力","desc":"資產回報率持續擴張 (ΔROA > 0)","passed":1,"detail":"回報率穩步領先同業基準"},{"id":4,"category":"盈利能力","desc":"應計利潤品質高 (CFO > 淨利潤)","passed":0,"detail":"真實現金流充沛，無虛報帳面獲利"},{"id":5,"category":"槓桿與償債","desc":"財務槓桿未惡化 (ΔLeverage ≤ 0)","passed":1,"detail":"總負債資產比率 = 57.0%"},{"id":6,"category":"槓桿與償債","desc":"短期流動性安全 (ΔLiquidity > 0)","passed":0,"detail":"流動比率 = 0.46"},{"id":7,"category":"槓桿與償債","desc":"股本未遭稀釋 (ΔShares ≤ 0)","passed":1,"detail":"未大幅增發新股割韭菜"},{"id":8,"category":"營運效率","desc":"毛利率擴張 (ΔMargin > 0)","passed":1,"detail":"產品定價權增強，毛利結構健康"},{"id":9,"category":"營運效率","desc":"資產週轉率提升 (ΔTurnover > 0)","passed":1,"detail":"每單位資產產出效益改善"}],"fair_val":112.78,"default_fair_val":112.78,"premium_pct":49.1,"is_undervalued":false,"pe_trailing":26.7,"pe_forward":23.5,"pb_trailing":7.1,"pb_forward":6.4,"div_yield":1.71,"ps_ratio":6.8,"fcf_to_ev":3.41,"fcf_to_mcap":3.68,"liab_to_assets":57,"cash_to_assets":5.5,"current_ratio":0.46,"roe":26.5,"roa":11.3,"moat":{"ticker":"TXRH","period":"2026Q2","m1_brand_pricing":{"score":7,"comment_zh":"Texas Roadhouse 建立了一個強大的品牌形象，以其休閒的用餐氛圍、份量十足的餐點和相對實惠的價格吸引了廣泛的客群。雖然其定價權不如頂級餐飲品牌，但在其細分市場中，其品牌價值足以支撐其定價策略，並在一定程度上抵禦價格競爭。其「手作」和「在地」的品牌故事，以及持續的菜單創新，有助於維持顧客忠誠度和品牌溢價，但仍需面對來自其他連鎖餐廳和獨立餐廳的激烈競爭。","comment_en":"Texas Roadhouse has cultivated a strong brand identity, attracting a broad customer base with its casual dining atmosphere, generous portions, and relatively affordable pricing. While its pricing power isn't on par with premium brands, within its segment, its brand value supports its pricing strategy and offers some resilience against price competition. The 'hand-crafted' and 'local' brand narrative, coupled with ongoing menu innovation, helps maintain customer loyalty and a degree of premium, though it faces intense competition from other chains and independent restaurants."},"m2_patents_regulatory":{"score":1,"comment_zh":"餐飲業的進入門檻相對較低，Texas Roadhouse 並不依賴專利或獨特的監管壁壘。其競爭優勢主要來自營運和品牌，而非知識產權。雖然食品安全和衛生法規是必須遵守的，但這些標準對所有業者都是一致的，不構成獨特的競爭優勢。因此，此維度的護城河極為薄弱。","comment_en":"The restaurant industry has relatively low barriers to entry, and Texas Roadhouse does not rely on patents or unique regulatory moats. Its competitive advantages stem primarily from operations and branding, not intellectual property. While food safety and health regulations are mandatory, these standards apply uniformly to all operators and do not confer a unique competitive advantage. Therefore, the moat in this dimension is extremely weak."},"m3_high_switching_costs":{"score":4,"comment_zh":"顧客轉換至其他餐廳的成本非常低，因為用餐體驗的選擇眾多且易於取得。然而，Texas Roadhouse 透過其獨特的用餐體驗、忠誠度計畫（如禮品卡和特定促銷活動）以及習慣養成，在一定程度上增加了顧客回訪的意願。但這種連結相對較弱，一旦有更具吸引力的替代選擇出現，顧客仍可能轉移。","comment_en":"The cost for customers to switch to other restaurants is very low, given the abundance and accessibility of dining options. However, Texas Roadhouse fosters some degree of customer stickiness through its unique dining experience, loyalty programs (like gift cards and specific promotions), and habit formation. This connection is relatively weak, and customers may still switch if more compelling alternatives arise."},"m4_network_effects":{"score":1,"comment_zh":"Texas Roadhouse 的商業模式不具備顯著的網絡效應。其成功更多地依賴於單一餐廳的營運效率、品牌吸引力和選址。顧客的用餐體驗不會因為其他顧客的加入而顯著提升，公司也無法從用戶數量的增加中獲得指數級的優勢。因此，此維度的護城河幾乎不存在。","comment_en":"Texas Roadhouse's business model does not exhibit significant network effects. Its success relies more on the operational efficiency of individual restaurants, brand appeal, and location. The dining experience for a customer does not inherently improve with more customers, nor does the company gain an exponential advantage from user growth. Consequently, the moat in this dimension is virtually non-existent."},"m5_cost_advantage_scale":{"score":7,"comment_zh":"作為一個大型連鎖餐廳，Texas Roadhouse 受惠於規模經濟。其龐大的採購量使其在食材、設備和供應鏈管理上能獲得比小型獨立餐廳更優惠的價格。這種採購優勢有助於維持其相對較低的價格點，同時保持一定的利潤率。此外，標準化的營運流程和後勤支持也降低了單店的營運成本。","comment_en":"As a large restaurant chain, Texas Roadhouse benefits from economies of scale. Its substantial purchasing volume allows for more favorable pricing on ingredients, equipment, and supply chain management compared to smaller independent restaurants. This purchasing advantage helps maintain its relatively affordable price points while preserving profit margins. Furthermore, standardized operational processes and logistical support reduce per-unit operating costs."},"m6_unique_geography_assets":{"score":2,"comment_zh":"Texas Roadhouse 的選址策略是其成長的關鍵，但其地理資產並非獨一無二或不可複製。公司傾向於在交通便利、人口密度適中的郊區或次級市場開設餐廳，這些地點的選擇有助於吸引目標客群。然而，這些地點並非絕對的壟斷，競爭對手也可能在相似的區域開設餐廳，因此地理位置帶來的壁壘相對有限。","comment_en":"Texas Roadhouse's site selection strategy is key to its growth, but its geographic assets are neither unique nor irreplicable. The company tends to open restaurants in suburban or secondary markets with convenient access and moderate population density, which helps attract its target demographic. However, these locations are not absolute monopolies, and competitors can also establish presence in similar areas, thus limiting the barrier provided by geography."},"m7_operational_efficiency":{"score":8,"comment_zh":"Texas Roadhouse 在營運效率方面表現出色，這是其核心競爭力之一。公司透過標準化的菜單、高效的廚房流程、精準的庫存管理和強大的供應鏈，實現了快速的翻桌率和穩定的餐點品質。其獨特的「前台」文化（如花生和麵包）不僅提升了顧客體驗，也有效利用了等待時間。這種高度優化的營運模式，是其能夠在競爭激烈的餐飲市場中脫穎而出的關鍵。","comment_en":"Texas Roadhouse excels in operational efficiency, which is one of its core competitive strengths. Through standardized menus, efficient kitchen workflows, precise inventory management, and a robust supply chain, the company achieves high table turnover rates and consistent food quality. Its distinctive 'front-porch' culture (e.g., peanuts and bread) not only enhances the customer experience but also effectively utilizes waiting times. This highly optimized operational model is crucial for its success in the competitive restaurant market."},"m8_capital_allocation":{"score":7,"comment_zh":"Texas Roadhouse 在資本配置方面展現了穩健的紀律。公司將大部分資本用於開設新店以擴張市場份額，同時也進行適度的股票回購和股息支付。其展店策略似乎能持續產生高於資本成本的回報，顯示其對新店選址和營運的判斷力。雖然其負債水平相對較高，但強勁的自由現金流使其能夠有效管理債務並支持成長。","comment_en":"Texas Roadhouse demonstrates sound discipline in capital allocation. The company primarily invests in opening new stores to expand market share, complemented by moderate share repurchases and dividend payments. Its expansion strategy appears to consistently generate returns above the cost of capital, indicating good judgment in site selection and operations for new locations. While its debt levels are relatively high, strong free cash flow enables effective debt management and supports growth."},"m9_customer_retention":{"score":7,"comment_zh":"Texas Roadhouse 透過提供一致的用餐體驗、誘人的菜單和熱情的服務，成功培養了高度的顧客忠誠度。其「家常菜」的氛圍和份量十足的餐點，讓顧客感到物有所值。雖然沒有複雜的會員系統，但其品牌吸引力和顧客習慣形成了穩固的回訪基礎。節日促銷和禮品卡等策略也進一步鞏固了顧客關係，使其在眾多餐飲選擇中保持競爭力。","comment_en":"Texas Roadhouse cultivates strong customer loyalty by consistently delivering a satisfying dining experience, appealing menu, and friendly service. Its 'homestyle' atmosphere and generous portions provide a sense of value for money. While not relying on complex loyalty programs, its brand appeal and customer habits form a solid base for repeat visits. Strategies like holiday promotions and gift cards further solidify customer relationships, maintaining its competitiveness amidst numerous dining options."},"m10_durability":{"score":6,"comment_zh":"Texas Roadhouse 的商業模式具有一定的持久性，其核心的休閒餐飲定位不易受到短期趨勢的劇烈影響。然而，餐飲業本身就面臨持續的競爭和消費者口味的變化。雖然其品牌和營運模式相對穩固，但長期來看，仍需不斷適應市場變化、創新菜單並維持高品質的服務，以應對潛在的顛覆性技術或新興的餐飲模式。","comment_en":"Texas Roadhouse's business model possesses a degree of durability; its core casual dining positioning is not easily swayed by short-term trends. However, the restaurant industry inherently faces constant competition and evolving consumer tastes. While its brand and operational model are relatively stable, long-term success requires continuous adaptation to market changes, menu innovation, and sustained high-quality service to counter potential disruptive technologies or emerging dining concepts."},"overall_moat_verdict_zh":"Texas Roadhouse 的護城河主要建立在其卓越的營運效率（M7）和規模經濟帶來的成本優勢（M5）之上，輔以穩固的品牌忠誠度（M9）和相對成功的展店策略（M8）。它在休閒餐飲領域建立了一個「收費橋」式的商業模式，透過標準化流程和規模採購，以具競爭力的價格提供穩定品質的餐點，吸引並留住大量顧客。然而，其護城河並非無懈可擊，缺乏專利或網絡效應（M2, M4），且轉換成本不高（M3），使其易受競爭影響。整體而言，它是一個在特定細分市場中運營良好的企業，但其護城河的深度和廣度相較於頂級的特許經營權或技術壁壘型企業仍有差距。","overall_moat_verdict_en":"Texas Roadhouse's moat is primarily built upon its exceptional operational efficiency (M7) and cost advantages derived from economies of scale (M5), supported by solid brand loyalty (M9) and a reasonably successful expansion strategy (M8). It operates a 'toll bridge'-like business model within the casual dining segment, leveraging standardized processes and bulk purchasing to offer consistent quality at competitive prices, thereby attracting and retaining a large customer base. However, its moat is not impenetrable, lacking patents or network effects (M2, M4), and facing low switching costs (M3), making it susceptible to competition. Overall, it's a well-operated business in its niche, but the depth and breadth of its moat are less formidable than those of top-tier franchise or technology-based moats.","evidenceHash":"3d00ac8fe288bffebeb66bede180ed4567453913d84a6e2b5841327c04c4368b","assessmentPolicy":"us-buffett-moat-v3"},"ratingSources":{"moat":{"reason":null},"fScore":{"score":7,"checkedAt":null},"zScore":{"asOfDate":"2025-12-30","period":"FY 2025","basis":"comparableAnnual","model":"z","zone":"superRobust","reason":null,"scoringCurrency":"USD","applicability":null,"checkedAt":"2026-10-28T14:40:26.418Z","evidenceHash":"a16b6164cdb736930ce85c9bc860390c22734694ea0dfc128d406d6050c38f21"},"mScore":{"asOfDate":"2025-12-30","period":"FY 2025","basis":"comparableAnnual","model":null,"zone":"clean","reason":null,"scoringCurrency":"USD","applicability":null,"checkedAt":"2026-10-28T14:40:26.418Z","evidenceHash":"a16b6164cdb736930ce85c9bc860390c22734694ea0dfc128d406d6050c38f21"}},"fin_valuation":{"is_financial":false},"image":"https://images.financialmodelingprep.com/symbol/TXRH.png","logo":"https://images.financialmodelingprep.com/symbol/TXRH.png","website":"https://www.texasroadhouse.com","ceo":"Gerald L. Morgan","full_time_employees":"101000","description":"Texas Roadhouse, Inc., through its various subsidiaries, is actively engaged in the casual dining sector, managing restaurants both within the United States and on a global scale. The company's portfolio encompasses establishments operating under its proprietary brands, which include Texas Roadhouse, Bubba's 33, and Jaggers, all of which it either directly runs or licenses to franchisees. By December 28, 2021, the firm reported overseeing 566 company-operated restaurants in the U.S., complemented by 101 franchised locations. Founded in 1993, Texas Roadhouse, Inc. maintains its corporate base in Louisville, Kentucky.","description_en":"Texas Roadhouse, Inc., through its various subsidiaries, is actively engaged in the casual dining sector, managing restaurants both within the United States and on a global scale. The company's portfolio encompasses establishments operating under its proprietary brands, which include Texas Roadhouse, Bubba's 33, and Jaggers, all of which it either directly runs or licenses to franchisees. By December 28, 2021, the firm reported overseeing 566 company-operated restaurants in the U.S., complemented by 101 franchised locations. Founded in 1993, Texas Roadhouse, Inc. maintains its corporate base in Louisville, Kentucky.","description_zh":"**德州牛排館公司 (Texas Roadhouse, Inc. - TXRH)**\n\n德州牛排館公司（Texas Roadhouse, Inc.）透過其子公司，深耕美國及全球的休閒餐飲市場。公司旗下營運的餐飲品牌包括其核心品牌 **Texas Roadhouse**，以及 **Bubba's 33** 和 **Jaggers**。這些品牌餐廳的營運模式涵蓋直營與授權加盟。截至2021年12月28日，公司於美國境內共經營566家直營餐廳，並有101家加盟據點。\n\n公司專注於提供高品質的牛排及美式餐點，以其獨特的「德州風格」用餐體驗著稱，強調現切牛排、手工麵包及花生等特色。營運模式上，德州牛排館以其標準化的菜單、嚴格的品質控管及具成本效益的採購策略，確保餐點的一致性與獲利能力。透過直營與加盟並行的策略，公司得以快速擴張市場版圖，同時維持品牌形象與營運效率。","address":"6040 Dutchmans Lane","city":"Louisville","state":"KY","zip":"40205","country":"US","phone":"502 426 9984","full_address":"6040 Dutchmans Lane, Louisville, KY 40205, US","range_52w":"153.82-216.3","year_high":216.3,"year_low":153.82,"all_time_high":0,"all_time_low":153.82,"inst_ownership_pct":null,"insider_ownership_pct":null,"top_holders":[],"insider_trades":[{"date":"2026-08-27","name":"Marshall Lloyd Paul","title":"officer: CHIEF GROWTH OFFICER","is_buy":false,"action":"S-Sale","shares":500,"price":204.65,"total_val":0.1},{"date":"2026-08-27","name":"Carroll Hugh J","title":"director","is_buy":false,"action":"S-Sale","shares":650,"price":203.99,"total_val":0.13},{"date":"2026-08-21","name":"Morgan Gerald L.","title":"director, officer: CEO, EXECUTIVE VICE CHAIRMAN","is_buy":false,"action":"S-Sale","shares":15000,"price":202.17,"total_val":3.03},{"date":"2026-08-21","name":"EPPS DONNA E","title":"director","is_buy":null,"action":"G-Gift","shares":49,"price":0,"total_val":0},{"date":"2026-08-19","name":"Humpich Keith","title":"officer: CHIEF ACCT & FIN SVCS OFFCR","is_buy":false,"action":"S-Sale","shares":819,"price":204.11,"total_val":0.17},{"date":"2026-08-19","name":"EPPS DONNA E","title":"director","is_buy":false,"action":"S-Sale","shares":820,"price":206.56,"total_val":0.17},{"date":"2026-08-19","name":"EPPS DONNA E","title":"director","is_buy":null,"action":"G-Gift","shares":49,"price":0,"total_val":0},{"date":"2026-08-13","name":"MOORE GREGORY N","title":"director","is_buy":false,"action":"S-Sale","shares":3000,"price":208.32,"total_val":0.62},{"date":"2026-07-06","name":"Humpich Keith","title":"officer: CHIEF ACCT & FIN SVCS OFFCR","is_buy":null,"action":"M-Exempt","shares":2114,"price":0,"total_val":0},{"date":"2026-07-06","name":"Humpich Keith","title":"officer: CHIEF ACCT & FIN SVCS OFFCR","is_buy":null,"action":"F-InKind","shares":636,"price":191.48,"total_val":0.12}],"stock_splits":[{"date":"2005-09-26","ratio":"2 : 1","desc":"供應商報告的股數調整比例；未獨立核實事件類型。","type":"FMP 股數調整"}],"fmp_symbol":"TXRH","real_